# ouroboros#142: the VM omits `_`-prefixed module bindings from the module
# dict; the AOT's dict carried every top-level binding, so `keys of
# <module>` and its length diverged and a program could reach private
# helpers through the dict. Filtered at the dict build only (the rename
# set still covers private names, which the public functions call).
import checksum
print of (keys of checksum)
print of (len of (keys of checksum))
print of (checksum.crc32 of "abc")
print of (has_key of [checksum, "_blen"])
